# Auto Scaling - Cloud Watch Alarms & Scaling

**CloudWatch** monitors metrics from your application and infrastructure, while the Auto Scaling Group **(ASG)** uses those metrics to automatically adjust the number of EC2 instances.

CloudWatch can monitor things such as:
- **CPU utilisation**
- memory usage
- other/custom application metrics

When a configured threshold is reached, a **CloudWatch Alarm** can trigger a scaling policy.

### Scaling Policies
- **Scale Out** — if demand becomes high, such as high CPU usage, the ASG launches more EC2 instances.
- **Scale In** — when demand drops, the ASG removes unnecessary instances to reduce costs.
```text
High CPU
   ↓
CloudWatch Alarm triggered
   ↓
Scaling Policy
   ↓
ASG adds EC2 instances


Low demand
   ↓
CloudWatch Alarm triggered
   ↓
Scaling Policy
   ↓
ASG removes EC2 instances
```
This combines monitoring + automation, allowing AWS to adjust capacity based on real-time demand.

### Key Idea
**CloudWatch watches the metrics → alarms detect conditions → scaling policies tell the ASG what action to take**.

This helps maintain performance during busy periods while reducing unnecessary costs when demand is low.